# No unwrap or expect

Never call `unwrap()` or `expect()` in Rust, including tests and “infallible” setup.

Use `?`, `match`, `if let`, `ok()`, or `unwrap_or` / `unwrap_or_else` / `unwrap_or_default`.

For `Mutex::lock()`, recover poison:

```rust
match m.lock() {
    Ok(g) => g,
    Err(p) => p.into_inner(),
}
```

In tests, fail with `assert!` or `let … else { panic!(…) }`, not `unwrap`/`expect`.
